WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:09.522
Hi! A pencil and an eraser: which is longer? Today we'll compare lengths and measure in centimetres.

2
00:00:09.672 --> 00:00:13.914
To compare, line up one end, then look at the other end.

3
00:00:14.064 --> 00:00:20.346
For two things say longer or shorter; for three or more, longest and shortest.

4
00:00:20.496 --> 00:00:23.706
For height, line up at the bottom too.

5
00:00:23.856 --> 00:00:30.354
We can measure with paper clips end to end: the pencil is 5 clips long.

6
00:00:30.504 --> 00:00:34.458
We measure short things in centimetres, written cm.

7
00:00:34.608 --> 00:00:38.490
Line one end of the object up with 0 on the ruler.

8
00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:42.546
The number at the other end is the length in centimetres.

9
00:00:42.696 --> 00:00:49.722
Longer minus shorter gives the difference: 12 minus 7 is 5 centimetres.

10
00:00:49.872 --> 00:00:53.970
Watch out! Line up with 0, not 1!

11
00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:57.642
Starting at 1 makes the reading 1 too many.

12
00:00:57.792 --> 00:01:01.530
So always start at 0.

13
00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:11.754
Your turn! With one end lined up, is the one that sticks out longer or shorter? Pause and think.

14
00:01:11.904 --> 00:01:17.346
The one that sticks out is longer. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:17.496 --> 00:01:28.002
Another one! Starting at 0, the other end is at 9. How long is it? Pause and think.

16
00:01:28.152 --> 00:01:34.218
It points to 9, so 9 centimetres. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:34.368 --> 00:01:47.154
Here's another! One string is 15 cm and another is 9 cm. How much longer is the long one? Pause and think.

18
00:01:47.304 --> 00:01:53.610
15 minus 9 is 6 centimetres. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:53.760 --> 00:02:06.306
Try one more! A is 8 cm, B is 12 cm and C is 5 cm. Which is longest? Pause and think.

20
00:02:06.456 --> 00:02:12.426
12 is the biggest, so B is longest. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:12.576 --> 00:02:21.450
Try one more! Same three. Which is shortest? Pause and think.

22
00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:27.618
5 is the smallest, so C is shortest. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:27.768 --> 00:02:38.466
Try one more! One pen is 6 clips long and another is 4. Which is longer? Pause and think.

24
00:02:38.616 --> 00:02:45.618
6 is more than 4, so the 6-clip pen is longer. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:45.768 --> 00:02:56.082
Last one! To measure how long a desk is, do we use centimetres or kilograms? Pause and think.

26
00:02:56.232 --> 00:03:01.434
Length uses centimetres. Did you get it right?

27
00:03:01.584 --> 00:03:09.258
Remember: line up one end to compare. With a ruler, start at 0 and read the other end in centimetres.

28
00:03:09.408 --> 00:03:13.410
Measure your pencil with a ruler!

